## 4. The Innovation Margin: Automation vs. Reinstatement

### 4.1 Directed Technical Change

A continuum of innovators of mass one chooses research effort between automation R&D (which raises \(\mathcal{A}_{j,t}\)) and reinstatement R&D (which creates new labor-intensive tasks \(n_t\)). Let \(z_t \in [0,1]\) be the share of research effort allocated to reinstatement. Profits from each activity exhibit diminishing returns to research effort:
\[
\Pi_{N,t} = \pi_N z_t^\phi \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta}, \qquad \Pi_{A,t} = \pi_A (1 - z_t)^\phi \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{\eta}, \qquad \eta > 0, \ \phi \in (0,1), \tag{27}
\]
where \(r_t\) is a weighted average of \(r_{C,t}\) and \(r_{P,t}\):
\[
r_t = \frac{\mathcal{A}_{C,t} Z_{C,t}}{\mathcal{A}_{C,t} Z_{C,t} + \mathcal{A}_{P,t} Z_{P,t}} r_{C,t} + \frac{\mathcal{A}_{P,t} Z_{P,t}}{\mathcal{A}_{C,t} Z_{C,t} + \mathcal{A}_{P,t} Z_{P,t}} r_{P,t}. \tag{28}
\]

The parameter \(\phi \in (0,1)\) captures diminishing returns to research effort. Without it, the profit functions are linear in \(z_t\), and the solution is a corner: \(z_t = 1\) if reinstatement is more profitable, \(z_t = 0\) otherwise. The interior solution requires \(\phi < 1\).

### 4.2 Equilibrium Allocation

Innovators equate marginal profits:
\[
\phi \pi_N z_t^{\phi-1} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta} = \phi \pi_A (1 - z_t)^{\phi-1} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{\eta}. \tag{29}
\]

Solving:
\[
\left(\frac{z_t}{1 - z_t}\right)^{\phi-1} = \frac{\pi_A}{\pi_N} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta}. \tag{30}
\]

Rearranging:
\[
\frac{z_t}{1 - z_t} = \left[ \frac{\pi_N}{\pi_A} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{2\eta} \right]^{\frac{1}{1-\phi}}. \tag{31}
\]

Therefore:
\[
z_t^* = \frac{\left[ \frac{\pi_N}{\pi_A} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{2\eta} \right]^{\frac{1}{1-\phi}}}{1 + \left[ \frac{\pi_N}{\pi_A} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{2\eta} \right]^{\frac{1}{1-\phi}}}. \tag{32}
\]

This is the reinstatement share. It is increasing in \(w_t/r_t\): when labor is relatively cheap, innovators allocate more effort to reinstatement.

**Reinstatement.** The mass of new labor-intensive tasks is:
\[
n_t = \bar{n} + \nu z_t^* \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta}, \qquad \nu > 0. \tag{33}
\]

This specification is bounded in \([\bar{n}, \bar{n} + \nu]\) and respects the comparative statics of directed technical change.

**Remark.** This block is explicitly a reduced-form representation of the innovation margin. It is not a fully dynamic model with forward-looking innovators, entry, uncertainty, or spillovers. It should be interpreted as a static approximation that captures the direction of innovative response to relative factor prices.

### 4.3 Net Displacement

Define net displacement as:
\[
D_t^{\text{net}} = \mathcal{A}_{C,t} + \mathcal{A}_{P,t} - n_t. \tag{34}
\]

The stabilizing force of reinstatement is microfounded: as automation displaces labor and pushes \(w_t / r_t\) down, \(z_t^*\) rises and \(n_t\) increases.

