## Appendix C: Derivation of the Reallocation Equation

### C.1 Task-Level Labor Demand

For a non-automated cognitive task \(i\), the unit cost is \(c_{\text{non-auto},t} = w_t/A_{L,t}\). From (A.22):
\[
l_t(i) = \frac{1}{A_{L,t}} y_t(i). \tag{C.1}
\]

The demand for task \(i\) is:
\[
y_t(i) = \left(\frac{\varepsilon}{\varepsilon-1} \frac{c_{\text{non-auto},t}}{P_t}\right)^{-\varepsilon} \frac{Y_t}{P_t}. \tag{C.2}
\]

Substituting:
\[
l_t(i) = \frac{1}{A_{L,t}} \left(\frac{\varepsilon}{\varepsilon-1} \frac{w_t}{A_{L,t} P_t}\right)^{-\varepsilon} \frac{Y_t}{P_t}. \tag{C.3}
\]

Under (A2), all non-automated cognitive tasks share the same unit cost. Aggregating over the mass \(N_{C,t}\):
\[
L_{C,t} = N_{C,t} \frac{1}{A_{L,t}} \left(\frac{\varepsilon}{\varepsilon-1} \frac{w_t}{A_{L,t} P_t}\right)^{-\varepsilon} \frac{Y_t}{P_t}. \tag{C.4}
\]

### C.2 Log-Linearization

Take logs:
\[
\ln L_{C,t} = \ln N_{C,t} - \ln A_{L,t} - \varepsilon \ln\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{\varepsilon-1}\right) - \varepsilon \ln w_t + \varepsilon \ln A_{L,t} + \varepsilon \ln P_t + \ln Y_t - \ln P_t. \tag{C.5}
\]

Differentiate:
\[
\hat{L}_{C,t} = \hat{N}_{C,t} - \hat{A}_{L,t} - \varepsilon \hat{w}_t + \varepsilon \hat{A}_{L,t} + \varepsilon \hat{P}_t + \hat{Y}_t - \hat{P}_t. \tag{C.6}
\]

Simplifying:
\[
\hat{L}_{C,t} = \hat{N}_{C,t} + \hat{Y}_t - \varepsilon \hat{w}_t + (\varepsilon - 1) \hat{A}_{L,t} + (\varepsilon - 1) \hat{P}_t. \tag{C.7}
\]

Under the maintained assumption that the price index moves proportionally with the unit cost of non-automated tasks \((\hat{P}_t = 0)\), this simplifies to:
\[
\hat{L}_{C,t} = \hat{N}_{C,t} + \hat{Y}_t - \varepsilon \hat{w}_t + (\varepsilon - 1) \hat{A}_{L,t}. \tag{C.8}
\]

Define the automation share:
\[
\varsigma_{C,t} = \frac{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}}{1 - \mathcal{A}_{C,t}}. \tag{C.9}
\]

Then \(\hat{N}_{C,t} = -\varsigma_{C,t} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}}\), and:
\[
\hat{L}_{C,t} = \hat{Y}_t - \varepsilon \hat{w}_t + (\varepsilon - 1) \hat{A}_{L,t} - \varsigma_{C,t} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}}. \tag{C.10}
\]

### C.3 Fixed Labor Supply

Labor supply is fixed: \(L_{C,t} + L_{I,t} = \bar{L}\), so:
\[
dL_{C,t} = -dL_{I,t}. \tag{C.11}
\]

Therefore:
\[
\Delta L_{I,t} = -\Delta L_{C,t} = -L_{C,t-1} \hat{L}_{C,t} = L_{C,t-1} \left[ \varsigma_{C,t} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}} + \varepsilon \hat{w}_t - (\varepsilon - 1) \hat{A}_{L,t} - \hat{Y}_t \right]. \tag{C.12}
\]

### C.4 Wage–Output Co-Movement

Under the maintained assumption \(\hat{w}_t \approx \hat{Y}_t\):
\[
\Delta L_{I,t} = L_{C,t-1} \left[ \varsigma_{C,t} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}} + (\varepsilon - 1) \hat{Y}_t - (\varepsilon - 1) \hat{A}_{L,t} \right]. \tag{C.13}
\]

This can be written as:
\[
\Delta L_{I,t} = L_{C,t-1} \left[ \varsigma_{C,t} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}} + (\varepsilon - 1)(\hat{Y}_t - \hat{A}_{L,t}) \right]. \tag{C.14}
\]

This is the corrected reallocation equation.

### C.5 The Two Forces

The change in interpersonal employment is driven by:

1. **Net displacement:** \(\varsigma_{C,t} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}} - \widehat{n_t}\).
2. **Labor released by augmentation:** \((\varepsilon - 1)(\hat{Y}_t - \hat{A}_{L,t})\).

If \(\varepsilon < 1\) (gross complementarity), then \((\varepsilon - 1) < 0\), so higher productivity growth relative to output growth reduces interpersonal employment. If \(\varepsilon > 1\) (gross substitutability), the opposite holds.

### C.6 Comparative Statics

\[
\frac{\partial \Delta L_{I,t}}{\partial \mathcal{A}_{C,t}} = L_{C,t-1} \frac{\partial \varsigma_{C,t}}{\partial \mathcal{A}_{C,t}} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}} > 0, \tag{C.15}
\]
since \(\varsigma_{C,t}\) is increasing in \(\mathcal{A}_{C,t}\).

\[
\frac{\partial \Delta L_{I,t}}{\partial n_t} = -L_{C,t-1} \frac{\partial \widehat{N}_{C,t}}{\partial n_t} < 0, \tag{C.16}
\]
since reinstatement raises \(N_{C,t}\) and reduces the need for reallocation.

\[
\frac{\partial \Delta L_{I,t}}{\partial A_{L,t}} = -L_{C,t-1} (\varepsilon - 1) \gtrless 0 \quad \text{as} \quad \varepsilon \lessgtr 1. \tag{C.17}
\]

\[
\frac{\partial \Delta L_{I,t}}{\partial \varepsilon} = L_{C,t-1} (\hat{Y}_t - \hat{A}_{L,t}) \gtrless 0 \quad \text{as} \quad \hat{Y}_t \gtrless \hat{A}_{L,t}. \tag{C.18}
\]

