## Appendix G: Static Directed Technical Change (Corrected)

### G.1 The Innovator's Problem

A representative innovator chooses \(z_t \in [0,1]\) to maximize:
\[
\max_{z_t} \ \Pi_t = \pi_N z_t^\phi \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta} + \pi_A (1 - z_t)^\phi \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{\eta}, \qquad \phi \in (0,1). \tag{G.1}
\]

The parameter \(\phi \in (0,1)\) captures diminishing returns to research effort.

### G.2 First-Order Condition

\[
\frac{\partial \Pi_t}{\partial z_t} = \phi \pi_N z_t^{\phi-1} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta} - \phi \pi_A (1 - z_t)^{\phi-1} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{\eta} = 0. \tag{G.2}
\]

### G.3 Solution

Dividing by \(\phi\):
\[
\pi_N z_t^{\phi-1} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta} = \pi_A (1 - z_t)^{\phi-1} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{\eta}. \tag{G.3}
\]

Rearranging:
\[
\left(\frac{z_t}{1 - z_t}\right)^{\phi-1} = \frac{\pi_A}{\pi_N} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta}. \tag{G.4}
\]

Solving for \(z_t^*\):
\[
\frac{z_t}{1 - z_t} = \left[ \frac{\pi_N}{\pi_A} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{2\eta} \right]^{\frac{1}{1-\phi}}. \tag{G.5}
\]

Therefore:
\[
z_t^* = \frac{\left[ \frac{\pi_N}{\pi_A} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{2\eta} \right]^{\frac{1}{1-\phi}}}{1 + \left[ \frac{\pi_N}{\pi_A} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{2\eta} \right]^{\frac{1}{1-\phi}}}. \tag{G.6}
\]

This is the reinstatement share. It is increasing in \(w_t/r_t\): when labor is relatively cheap, innovators allocate more effort to reinstatement.

### G.4 Comparative Statics

\[
\frac{\partial z_t^*}{\partial (w_t/r_t)} > 0, \qquad \frac{\partial z_t^*}{\partial (\pi_N/\pi_A)} > 0. \tag{G.7}
\]

### G.5 Reinstatement

The mass of new labor-intensive tasks is:
\[
n_t = \bar{n} + \nu z_t^* \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta}, \qquad \nu > 0. \tag{G.8}
\]

This is bounded in \([\bar{n}, \bar{n} + \nu]\) and respects the comparative statics of directed technical change.

### G.6 Dynamic Extension (Sketch)

A fully dynamic version would replace the static profit functions with:
\[
\Pi_{N,t} = \mathbb{E}_t \sum_{s=t}^\infty \beta^{s-t} \pi_{N,s} z_s^\phi \left(\frac{w_s}{r_s}\right)^{\eta}, \tag{G.9}
\]
\[
\Pi_{A,t} = \mathbb{E}_t \sum_{s=t}^\infty \beta^{s-t} \pi_{A,s} (1 - z_s)^\phi \left(\frac{r_s}{w_s}\right)^{\eta}. \tag{G.10}
\]

The first-order condition becomes an Euler equation:
\[
\phi \pi_{N,t} z_t^{\phi-1} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta} + \beta \mathbb{E}_t \frac{\partial V_{N,t+1}}{\partial z_t} = \phi \pi_{A,t} (1 - z_t)^{\phi-1} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{\eta} + \beta \mathbb{E}_t \frac{\partial V_{A,t+1}}{\partial z_t}. \tag{G.11}
\]

This is left for future research.

