## Diagram 3: Dual-Capital Production and Labor Share (Proposition 1)

```
TASK-LEVEL PRODUCTION:

  Cognitive task i in C:
    y_t(i) = [ (1-alpha_C,i)(A_L,t l_t(i))^((sigma_C-1)/sigma_C)
               + alpha_C,i (A_C,t k_C,t(i))^((sigma_C-1)/sigma_C) ]^(sigma_C/(sigma_C-1))

  Physical task i in P:
    y_t(i) = [ (1-alpha_P,i)(A_L,t l_t(i))^((sigma_P-1)/sigma_P)
               + alpha_P,i (A_P,t k_P,t(i))^((sigma_P-1)/sigma_P) ]^(sigma_P/(sigma_P-1))

  Interpersonal task i in I:
    y_t(i) = A_L,t l_t(i)

UNIT COST (j in {C,P}):
  c_t(i) = [ (1-alpha_{j,i})^sigma_j (w_t/A_L,t)^(1-sigma_j)
             + alpha_{j,i}^sigma_j (r_j,t/A_j,t)^(1-sigma_j) ]^(1/(1-sigma_j))

LABOR COST SHARE:
  s_L,t(i) = (1-alpha_{j,i})^sigma_j (w_t/A_L,t)^(1-sigma_j)
             / [ (1-alpha_{j,i})^sigma_j (w_t/A_L,t)^(1-sigma_j)
                 + alpha_{j,i}^sigma_j (r_j,t/A_j,t)^(1-sigma_j) ]

BINARY AUTOMATION CORNERS:
  alpha = 0  =>  c_t(i) = w_t/A_L,t  =>  s_L,t(i) = 1
  alpha = 1  =>  c_t(i) = r_j,t/A_j,t  =>  s_L,t(i) = 0

  ==> sigma_j DROPS OUT at corners

AGGREGATE OUTPUT (CES over tasks):
  Y_t = [ (1/M_t) integral_0^{M_t} y_t(i)^((epsilon-1)/epsilon) di ]^(epsilon/(epsilon-1))

AGGREGATE PRICE INDEX:
  P_t = [ (N_t/M_t) c_non-auto,t^(1-epsilon)
          + (A_C,t/M_t) c_C,auto,t^(1-epsilon)
          + (A_P,t/M_t) c_P,auto,t^(1-epsilon) ]^(1/(1-epsilon))

  where c_non-auto,t = w_t/A_L,t
        c_j,auto,t   = r_j,t/A_j,t

SHEPHARD'S LEMMA ON PRICE INDEX:
  s_L,t = (w_t/P_t) * (dP_t/dw_t)

  dP_t/dw_t = P_t^epsilon * (N_t/M_t) * (w_t/A_L,t)^(-epsilon) * (1/A_L,t)

  ==> s_L,t = (N_t/M_t) (w_t/A_L,t)^(1-epsilon) P_t^(epsilon-1)

SUBSTITUTE P_t^(epsilon-1) FROM PRICE INDEX:

  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  |                                                                                 |
