## Diagram 4: Labor Demand and Reallocation Equation (Corrected)

```
TASK-LEVEL LABOR DEMAND (CORRECTED):

  From Shephard's lemma:
    l_t(i) = (d c_t(i)/d w_t) * y_t(i)

  For non-automated task (alpha=0):
    c_t(i) = w_t/A_L,t
    d c_t(i)/d w_t = 1/A_L,t
    => l_t(i) = (1/A_L,t) y_t(i)

  Task demand:
    y_t(i) = ( (epsilon/(epsilon-1)) c_t(i)/P_t )^(-epsilon) * Y_t/P_t

  => l_t(i) = (1/A_L,t) * ( (epsilon/(epsilon-1)) w_t/(A_L,t P_t) )^(-epsilon) * Y_t/P_t

  OMITTED IN EARLIER FORMULATIONS:
    The factor c_t(i)^sigma / A_L,t
    => This factor is what makes sigma drop out and epsilon remain.

AGGREGATION OVER NON-AUTOMATED COGNITIVE TASKS:

  L_C,t = N_C,t * (1/A_L,t) * ( (epsilon/(epsilon-1)) w_t/(A_L,t P_t) )^(-epsilon) * Y_t/P_t

  Elasticity w.r.t. wage: -epsilon  (NOT -sigma)

LOG-LINEARIZATION:

  L_hat_C,t = N_hat_C,t + Y_hat_t - epsilon w_hat_t + (epsilon-1) A_hat_L,t + (epsilon-1) P_hat_t

  Under P_hat_t = 0:

  L_hat_C,t = Y_hat_t - epsilon w_hat_t + (epsilon-1) A_hat_L,t - varsigma_C,t A_hat_C,t

  where varsigma_C,t = A_C,t / (1 - A_C,t)

FIXED LABOR SUPPLY:

  L_C,t + L_I,t = L_bar  =>  dL_C,t = -dL_I,t

  Delta L_I,t = -Delta L_C,t = -L_C,t-1 L_hat_C,t

  => Delta L_I,t = L_C,t-1 [ varsigma_C,t A_hat_C,t + epsilon w_hat_t
                             - (epsilon-1) A_hat_L,t - Y_hat_t ]

WAGE-OUTPUT CO-MOVEMENT (w_hat_t = Y_hat_t):

  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  |                                                                                 |
  |   CORRECTED REALLOCATION EQUATION:                                              |
  |                                                                                 |
  |   Delta L_I,t = L_C,t-1 [ varsigma_C,t A_hat_C,t                                |
  |                            - (epsilon-1)(A_hat_L,t - Y_hat_t) ]                 |
  |                                                                                 |
  |   Or equivalently:                                                              |
  |                                                                                 |
  |   Delta L_I,t = L_C,t-1 [ varsigma_C,t A_hat_C,t                                |
  |                            + (epsilon-1)(Y_hat_t - A_hat_L,t) ]                 |
  |                                                                                 |
  |   Two forces:                                                                   |
  |     1. Net displacement: varsigma_C,t A_hat_C,t - n_hat_t                       |
  |     2. Augmentation effect: (epsilon-1)(Y_hat_t - A_hat_L,t)                    |
  |                                                                                 |
  |   SIGN OF AUGMENTATION EFFECT:                                                  |
  |     epsilon < 1 (gross complementarity): NEGATIVE                               |
  |     epsilon > 1 (gross substitutability): POSITIVE                              |
  |                                                                                 |
  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

COMPARATIVE STATICS:

  d Delta L_I,t / d A_C,t > 0     (more automation => more reallocation)
  d Delta L_I,t / d n_t   < 0     (more reinstatement => less reallocation)
  d Delta L_I,t / d A_L,t = -L_C,t-1 (epsilon-1)  (sign depends on epsilon)
  d Delta L_I,t / d epsilon = L_C,t-1 (Y_hat_t - A_hat_L,t)  (sign depends on Y vs A_L)
